Article 9 (Education on Emergency Rescue)
(1) The courses of education on emergency rescue under the former part of Article 55 (3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "emergency rescue education") and the hours of instruction for each course shall be as follows:
1. Course for managers responsible for emergency rescue duties: At least seven hours;
2. Course for practitioners responsible for emergency rescue duties: At least 14 hours;
3. Other courses deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard: Hours determined by the Commissioner General.
(2) Emergency rescue education under paragraph (1) shall cover the following subjects:
1. Policy directions and crisis management measures concerning responses to disasters occurring at sea;
2. Administrative practice concerning responses to disasters occurring at sea;
3. Theories and techniques concerning responses to emergency disasters occurring at sea;
4. Life-saving and first-aid methods necessary for emergency rescue activities;
5. Response methods for special disasters, such as marine pollution accidents and the sinking of large vessels;
6. Other matters deemed necessary by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.
(3) Where the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard intends to designate an educational institution to provide emergency rescue education under Article 55 (4) of the Act, the Commissioner General may request the head of the institution to submit a plan for operating emergency rescue education courses.
(4) Detailed matters necessary for operating emergency rescue education, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (3), shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Commissioner General of the Korea Coast Guard.
